{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>ידכה</b> — Thus is the way of the lion when it wishes to seize prey without being known: then it will pounce upon its prey." "<b>בעצומיו</b> — His hands and feet, which have mighty and ready strength. As we find יגרם [which means] ישבר גרם, and it is from the heavy [binyan], and we find likewise from the light [binyan]: לא גרמו לבקר. Behold, עצם [in the singular], and the plural עצמו from the heavy [binyan]; also it can be from the light [binyan], and behold the sense of בעצומיו would be: those who break bones." "<b>וחלכאים</b> — I have explained it [elsewhere]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "Ibn Ezra cites grammatical parallels: יגרם (Job 4:20) parsed as heavy binyan meaning 'he breaks a bone,' contrasted with לא גרמו לבקר (Genesis 31:39) in the light binyan meaning 'they did not break.' The reading עצמו is singular form cited alongside עצם; the final clause proposes reading the word as 'bone-breakers' from a root עצם II = שבר."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:59.328483963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}